BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:berkeley:20261110T190000Z-337070@events.berkeley.edu
SEQUENCE:0
DTSTAMP:20261108T053351Z
DTSTART:20261110T190000Z
DTEND:20261110T200000Z
SUMMARY:BIDS Seminar with Sylvain Corlay and Jeremy Tuloup of QuantStack
LOCATION:2300 Hearst Ave.\, Berkeley\, CA 94720
DESCRIPTION:Please join us for a special event with Gaël Varoquaux (Proba
 bl (https://probabl.ai/)\, scikit-learn (https://scikit-learn.org/stable/)
 )\, co-sponsored by BIDS\, CDSS\, and the Department of Statistics! Varoqu
 aux will give a 30-minute talk\, introduced by Fernando Pérez (https://bi
 ds.berkeley.edu/people/fernando-perez) (BIDS Faculty Director)\, followed 
 by a panel discussion on AI in open source and open science (https://blog.
 probabl.ai/maintaining-open-source-age-of-gen-ai) with Varoquaux\, Pérez\
 , and moderator Jarrod Millman (https://bids.berkeley.edu/people/jarrod-mi
 llman). → To attend in person: Register on this page. → To attend onli
 ne: Sign up here to receive a Zoom link (https://forms.gle/fKjzxbKFScfAMxk
 s5).Abstract Scikit-learn is the industry standard for machine-learning. I
  will share how we are seamlessly evolving its functionality\, making it e
 asier to use\, more powerful (e.g.\, with GPU support). Beyond exposing ma
 chine-learning algorithms\, a value of scikit-learn is that it shapes a st
 andard machine-learning API\, central to data science. I will introduce co
 mplementary packages that build upon this API to push the agenda:skrub (ht
 tps://skrub-data.org/stable/)\, bridging machine-learning and dataframe ma
 nipulation skore (https://probabl.ai/skore)\, to track and understand mach
 ine-learning work TabICL (https://arxiv.org/abs/2502.05564)\, an open mode
 l that implements tabular learning state of the art: table foundation mode
 ls This work is spurred by Probabl and a broader community\, and I'll expl
 ain our vision of sustainability for the ecosystem.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://luma.com/gn1niud2
END:VEVENT
